From 806aba6bfb0480e783ad69a8755a082a49fd8361 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:33:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] gated delta rule (metal): conv, norms and gates in the
 kernels with precise math

The first Metal path passed its self-check (7 tokens, max rel 5.4e-7) but failed two GPU cases
of delta_rule_tests on macos-15 (gpu_matches_f64_reference: out / state within 2e-5 of the f64
reference; half_inputs: state within 2e-5 of the CPU kernel): the library was built with fast
math and the conv / SiLU / L2 norms ran as candle tensor ops (also fast math), so the error of
exp(g) compounded through the per-token decay.

Now two kernels built without fast math, using precise exp / log / divide / sqrt: gdn_conv_f32
(conv over [conv_state ; tokens] + bias, SiLU) and gdn_scan_f32 (q / k squared norms reduced in
the threadgroup, gates with an accurate log1p, and the CPU kernel's update order per token:
S *= exp(g); m = S^T k; d = beta (v - m); S += k d^T; o = S^T q). Tensor ops only copy (dtype,
new conv state).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GcxyAs2y3NUizfXh9YWmxx
